## ⚙️ 7. Internal Working

Take this function:

```javascript
function greet() {
    console.log(this.name);
}
```

### 🚫 Without explicit binding

```javascript
greet();
```

JavaScript's internal decision process:

```
Was it called with `new`?
        │
        ▼  No
Was there an object before the dot?
        │
        ▼  No
✔ Use DEFAULT binding
```

### ✅ With explicit binding

```javascript
greet.call(person);
```

```
Was call() used?
        │
        ▼  Yes
Use the object passed to call()
        │
        ▼
this = person
        │
        ▼
🚀 Execute function
```

> 🔑 **Explicit binding OVERRIDES the default decision.**

---

## 🤖 8. JavaScript Engine Thinking

The engine roughly thinks like this:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["📞 Function Call"] --> B{"How was it called?"}
    B --> C["new binding?"]
    B --> D["Explicit binding? (call/apply/bind)"]
    B --> E["Implicit binding? (obj.fn())"]
    B --> F["Default binding"]
    C --> G["🎯 Assign this"]
    D --> G
    E --> G
    F --> G
    G --> H["▶️ Execute Function"]
```

> 🧘 **Don't memorise dozens of rules. Train yourself to think like the engine.**
>
> Whenever you see a function call, ask:
> **"How is this function being invoked?"**
>
> Answer that → determining `this` becomes straightforward.

